# AutoDQA AgentCore Runtime — environment for LOCAL testing (`agentcore launch -l`).
# In the cloud, set the SECRET values from AWS Secrets Manager (see README), and
# the non-secret identifiers as plain runtime env vars.
#
# EVERY VALUE BELOW IS A PLACEHOLDER. Fill them from the deployment you are
# targeting — do NOT expect these to work as-is. This file previously carried the
# real identifiers of a now-retired personal AWS/Cloudflare account, which meant a
# fresh copy silently pointed at the wrong stack. Placeholders instead of a second
# set of real values, deliberately: a wrong value should fail loudly, not connect
# to something plausible.
#
# The institutional deployment lives in AWS account 202102860812 (BigARC), profile
# `bigarc-autodqa`. Take the AgentCore/Cognito values from the
# .gateway_config.json written by agentcore-gateway/setup_gateway.py.

# --- Bedrock via the Cloudflare AI Gateway (BYOK) ------------------------------
# The gateway holds the AWS IAM SigV4 keys; the container only sends the token.
# Its BYOK must point at a Claude-enabled Bedrock account.
#
# Take these from the live agentcore-runtime/.env rather than from any other file in
# this repo. CF_AIG_TOKEN is scoped to one Cloudflare account and returns 401 against
# any other, so account id / gateway name / token must come from the same place. Note
# orchestrator-worker/wrangler.jsonc names a DIFFERENT account+gateway pair; that
# Worker is retired and its values should not be treated as current.
CF_ACCOUNT_ID=<cloudflare-account-id>
CF_AIG_GATEWAY=<cloudflare-ai-gateway-name>
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
CF_AIG_TOKEN=            # SECRET — cf-aig-authorization bearer

# --- AgentCore Gateway (MCP) + Cognito OAuth ---------------------------------
# The Runtime and the Gateway MUST live in the SAME AWS account, or run-microvm
# fails with a cross-account AccessDeniedException on the sandbox image.
# Copy these four from agentcore-gateway/.gateway_config.json after deploying.
AGENTCORE_GATEWAY_URL=https://<gateway-id>.gateway.bedrock-agentcore.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/mcp
COGNITO_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://<cognito-domain-prefix>.auth.us-east-1.amazoncognito.com/oauth2/token
COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=<cognito-app-client-id>
COGNITO_SCOPE=autodqa-gateway/invoke
COGNITO_CLIENT_SECRET=  # SECRET — Cognito app client secret
